The original DiffPDF upstream (Mark Summerfield, Qtrac Ltd.) went
proprietary after 2.1.3, the last free release.  Debian followed an
unofficial Qt 5 fork (https://gitlab.com/eang/diffpdf) for a while, and
since 1:1.0.6-1 packages disparPDF (https://github.com/yuw/disparPDF),
a Qt 6 port of ConfrontaPDF, which is itself a fork of DiffPDF.  Its
version numbers restart, hence the epoch; the source package keeps the
name diffpdf, and the binary package diffpdf is a transitional package
for disparpdf.

debian/patches are commits not yet in a disparPDF release, from the
disparpdf-fixes-and-features branch of https://github.com/barak/disparPDF
(offered upstream), exported with gbp pq.  Quilt patches cannot add
binary files, so the PDFs that the tests use, test/data/*.pdf, are left
out of the patches and kept in debian/test-data (listed in
debian/source/include-binaries); debian/rules copies them into place.
Drop debian/test-data once upstream has them.

Beware a textconv diff driver for PDFs in your git configuration (e.g.,
diff.pdf.textconv = pdftotext): format-patch, and so gbp pq export,
applies it, turning added PDFs into their text.

 -- Barak A. Pearlmutter <bap@debian.org>, Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0100
